Troubleshooting and Recovery

Failure Mode: Context Drift. If the agent loses its macro-goal, trigger a "Full Re-injection" where the parent plan is explicitly pushed back into the context window.

Failure Mode: Model Hallucination. If the Stability Daemon flags a high Lipschitz constant, switch to a conservative robust control policy (e.g., MPC with large safety margins).

Failure Mode: Safety Intervention. If the BCBF-QP filter is active more than 20% of the time, initiate an "Adaptive Safety Margin" update to learn that the environment is more dangerous than modeled.

